{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams"],"declarations":21,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.descending_witness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.descending_witness","kind":"theorem","line":315,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MFWSkeinInduction.lean#L315-L326","doc":"**The base case produces a witness.** For a descending `n`-strand word with\n`c` closure components the closure is the `c`-component unlink, whose HOMFLY\n`v`-degrees span `[-(c-1), c-1]`; with `DescendingWrithe` those endpoints lie in\nthe window, so the base case of the induction lands in the type the consequences\nfile consumes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.braid_bound_of_window","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.braid_bound_of_window","kind":"theorem","line":307,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MFWSkeinInduction.lean#L307-L313","doc":"The wiring is load-bearing: the braid-index bound now follows for anything\nthe induction produces, by `MortonFranksWilliams.braid_bound` rather than by a\nsecond copy of the argument. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.toWitness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.toWitness","kind":"def","line":293,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MFWSkeinInduction.lean#L293-L305","doc":"Build the witness `MortonFranksWilliams` consumes from two window\nmemberships — the shape the skein induction actually produces. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.spread_le_of_window","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.spread_le_of_window","kind":"theorem","line":274,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MFWSkeinInduction.lean#L274-L282","doc":"The spread bound `MortonFranksWilliams.braid_bound` consumes: the window\nhas width `2n − 2`, so `dmax − dmin ≤ 2n − 2`, i.e. `spread/2 + 1 ≤ n`. This\nis the bridge from the window to the braid-index statement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.descending_trivial_perm_writhe_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.descending_trivial_perm_writhe_zero","kind":"theorem","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MFWSkeinInduction.lean#L265-L272","doc":"The `c = n` corner the measurement singles out: a descending word whose\npermutation is trivial is forced to writhe **zero**. Recorded because it is the\nsharpest consequence of the hypothesis and the easiest place to look for a\ncounterexample. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.base_tight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.base_tight","kind":"theorem","line":258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MFWSkeinInduction.lean#L258-L263","doc":"Tightness, recorded because the measurement found it: at `|e| = n − c` the\nunlink's extreme degree sits exactly **on** the window edge. So the base case\nhas no slack either — combined with `switch_shift_eq` / `smooth_shift_eq`,\nnothing anywhere in this route wastes room, which is why MFW is sharp. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.base_window_of_descending","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.base_window_of_descending","kind":"theorem","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MFWSkeinInduction.lean#L247-L256","doc":"**The base case, given the hypothesis.** If `|e| ≤ n − c`, then every\n`v`-degree of the unlink term `δ^{c-1}` lies in the MFW window. This is the\nstep that makes `DescendingWrithe` load-bearing rather than decorative: it is\nused, not merely stated. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.DescendingWrithe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.DescendingWrithe","kind":"def","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MFWSkeinInduction.lean#L241-L245","doc":"The base-case hypothesis, named so it can be discharged later rather than\nre-invented: a totally descending `n`-strand word with `c` closure components\nhas `|e| ≤ n − c`. Classical — see the module docstring: descending ⇒ unlink\n(`lickorish1997`) plus Bennequin's inequality (`bennequin1983`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.smooth_shift_surj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.smooth_shift_surj","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MFWSkeinInduction.lean#L148-L152","doc":"The converse direction for the smoothing branch. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.switch_shift_surj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.switch_shift_surj","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MFWSkeinInduction.lean#L141-L146","doc":"The converse direction of `switch_shift`: every parent degree is reachable\nfrom the switch child. Together with `switch_shift` this is the bijection. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.shifts_preserve_width","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.shifts_preserve_width","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MFWSkeinInduction.lean#L133-L139","doc":"Consequence of the two above, and the reason MFW is **sharp**: neither\nskein branch loses any room at either edge, so the window the recursion\ndelivers is the window the base case starts with, shifted — never wider, never\nnarrower. Any slack in a computed spread therefore comes from the base case,\nnot from the recursion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.smooth_shift_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.smooth_shift_eq","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MFWSkeinInduction.lean#L127-L131","doc":"**The smoothing shift is a bijection of windows too.** Same correction:\n`1 + ((e−1) + n − 1) = e + n − 1` exactly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.switch_shift_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.switch_shift_eq","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MFWSkeinInduction.lean#L119-L125","doc":"**The switch shift is a bijection of windows, not merely an inclusion.**\n`v²·(window at e−2)` is *exactly* the window at `e`. I first recorded this as\nan inclusion with two units of slack at the top; that was wrong, and Lean\nrejected it — `2 + ((e−2) + n − 1) = e + n − 1`, not `e + n − 3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.smooth_tight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.smooth_tight","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MFWSkeinInduction.lean#L115-L117","doc":"The smoothing term is tight at the lower edge too. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.switch_tight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.switch_tight","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MFWSkeinInduction.lean#L108-L113","doc":"Both shifts are **tight at the lower edge**: the switch term realises\n`e − n + 1` exactly when the child does. This is why MFW is sharp, and it is\nthe reason `spread = 6` with `n = 4` forced the `6₁` writhe in\n`QOU.Knot.MortonFranksWilliams`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.mfw_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.mfw_step","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MFWSkeinInduction.lean#L96-L106","doc":"**The propagation step.** Every `v`-degree of `P₊ = v²P₋ + v z P₀` lies in\nthe parent window, given both children do. Stated on degrees rather than on\npolynomials: a degree of a sum is a degree of one of the summands, so this is\nthe whole content of the step. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.smooth_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.smooth_shift","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MFWSkeinInduction.lean#L89-L94","doc":"**Smoothing.** `P₀` sits at writhe `e − 1`; multiplying by `v·z` shifts its\nwindow into the parent's, also touching the lower edge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.switch_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.switch_shift","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MFWSkeinInduction.lean#L82-L87","doc":"**Crossing switch.** `P₋` sits at writhe `e − 2`; multiplying by `v²`\nshifts its window into the parent's, touching the lower edge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.window_nonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.window_nonempty","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MFWSkeinInduction.lean#L76-L80","doc":"The window is nonempty exactly when `1 ≤ n`: an `n`-strand braid always has\none. Recorded because a vacuous window would make everything below true for\nthe wrong reason. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.mem_window","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.mem_window","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MFWSkeinInduction.lean#L72-L74","doc":"Membership, unfolded. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.window","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MFWSkeinInduction.window","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MFWSkeinInduction.lean#L69-L70","doc":"The MFW `v`-degree window for an `n`-strand braid closure of writhe `e`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}